{"assignees":[],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nPressing `d` on a pull request (PR list or PR detail) switches to a \"PR diff window\": the changed files as a tree on the left and a side-by-side diff on the right, using the full width. `q` / `Esc` returns to the GitHub page with the previous selection intact.\n\n## Motivation\n\nThe GitHub page shows a PR's body, reviews and checks, but the actual change is only reachable through the browser. This lets you follow a PR's diff with the same feel as the Git page's diff view.\n\n## Design\n\n- **Navigation**: add `PageAction::Push(Box<dyn PageState>)` and give `App` a page stack. While a page is pushed, the header shows `PR #123 · feat/x → main · 12 files +340 −12` instead of the tab list; `q` / `Esc` pops it. The container is generic so commit diffs and worktree diffs can reuse it later.\n- **Panes**: reuse the Git page's `FileTreePane` and `DiffViewPane` as they are (they only take an `Rc<Vec<FileDiff>>`). Tree folding, search, the `i` vim mode and syntax highlighting keep working unchanged.\n- **Fetching the diff**: run `gh pr diff <n>` in the background and turn the patch into `FileDiff`s via `git2::Diff::from_buffer` → `files_from_diff` (the same path as the Worktrees page's stash preview). It is a REST call, so it costs no GraphQL quota and works for forks and unfetched branches. A PR too large for the API's diff limit becomes an error notice.\n- **Keys**: file_tree / diff_view keys are shared with the Git page. `e` opens the file in the editor only when it exists in the working tree. `o` opens the PR's Files tab in the browser, `y` copies that URL.\n- **Cache**: store the diff in `disk_cache` keyed by PR number so reopening is instant.\n- **KDL**: add `\"d\" \"ShowDiff\"` to `pr_list` and `detail_view` under `page \"github\"`. The diff window reuses the `file_tree` / `diff_view` keys of `page \"git\"`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `d` switches to the diff window; `q` / `Esc` returns to the previously selected PR\n- [ ] File tree and diff view interactions (folding / search / vim mode / horizontal scroll) behave as on the Git page\n- [ ] PRs from forks can be shown\n- [ ] `tape/demo-github-pr.tape` presses `d`, with a `pr_diff_<n>.out` fixture so the recording makes no API calls\n- [ ] README / README.ja / the guide (GitHub page chapter and Config Reference) are updated\n\n## Future work\n\n- When `origin/<head>` is already fetched, switch to a libgit2 tree-to-tree comparison (no size limit, works offline)\n- Show commit diffs from git_log and worktree diffs from the Worktrees page in the same window\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01N7wFSHbpTzvkK6WS1CRS7b","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-10-23T09:39:34Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":200,"state":"CLOSED","title":"GitHub page: show a PR's changed files and diff in a full-width window (`d`)"}
